{"id": "8cedf41a-78e0-42da-890c-d4fabc60e388", "question": "how is this used most often in histology?", "status": "ok", "num_iterations": 1, "total_delta_f": 0.9999999900000002, "total_step_score": 0.9999999900000002, "trajectory_quality_score": 0.9999999900000002, "steps": [{"iteration_index": 1, "retrieval_action": "text_retrieval_result", "retrieval_type": "Text Retrieval", "mode": "text_retrieval", "previous_query_for_similarity": null, "query": "Eosin dye in histology", "query_similarity_enabled": true, "query_similarity_with_previous": null, "similarity_threshold": 0.85, "fact_similarity_threshold": 0.9, "retrieval_index": 3, "reaction_index": 4, "reaction_action": "thought", "reaction_text": "The retrieved documents provide information about the use of Eosin in histology. Eosin is often used in conjunction with hematoxylin to stain tissues, with Eosin staining the basophilic components of cells red. It is commonly used in the H&E stain, which is a standard staining technique in histology. The H&E stain is used to visualize the structure of tissues and cells, making it easier to identify different types of cells and their characteristics.\n</Thought>", "facts_t": ["Eosinophils are dyed red by the acid stain, eosin.", "Basophils are dyed blue by the basic stain, hematoxylin."], "filtered_facts_t": ["Eosinophils are dyed red by the acid stain, eosin."], "accepted_facts_t": ["Eosinophils are dyed red by the acid stain, eosin."], "delta_f": 0.9999999900000002, "novel_facts": ["Eosinophils are dyed red by the acid stain, eosin."], "fact_novelty_matches": [{"fact": "Eosinophils are dyed red by the acid stain, eosin.", "is_novel": true, "duplicate_scope": null, "matched_fact": null, "matched_similarity": null}], "cumulative_fact_count_after_dedup": 1, "delta_reason": "set_difference", "utility_label": "full_contribution", "utility": 1.0, "utility_reason": "The reasoning clearly indicates that the retrieved evidence fully resolves the query about Eosin dye in histology by explaining its role, usage in H&E staining, and purpose.", "step_score": 0.9999999900000002}]}
{"id": "f17933a5-2975-4a36-bef8-fe102476953d", "question": "why does this help rabbit teeth?", "status": "ok", "num_iterations": 1, "total_delta_f": 0.9999999966666667, "total_step_score": 0.9999999966666667, "trajectory_quality_score": 0.9999999966666667, "steps": [{"iteration_index": 1, "retrieval_action": "text_retrieval_result", "retrieval_type": "Text Retrieval", "mode": "text_retrieval", "previous_query_for_similarity": null, "query": "benefits of Western Timothy Hay for rabbit teeth", "query_similarity_enabled": true, "query_similarity_with_previous": null, "similarity_threshold": 0.85, "fact_similarity_threshold": 0.9, "retrieval_index": 3, "reaction_index": 4, "reaction_action": "thought", "reaction_text": "The retrieved documents provide information about the benefits of Western Timothy Hay for rabbits. It is high in fiber and cellulose, which are important for digestive and dental health. The hay helps to prevent overgrowth of rabbit teeth by providing a natural abrasive that helps to wear down the teeth as the rabbit eats.\n</Thought>\nFinal Answer: Western Timothy Hay is high in fiber and cellulose, which are important for digestive and dental health in rabbits. The hay helps to prevent overgrowth of rabbit teeth by providing a natural abrasive that helps to wear down the teeth as the rabbit eats.", "facts_t": ["Rabbit teeth grow continuously throughout life.", "Rabbit teeth complement their diet.", "Rabbit diet consists of a wide range of vegetation.", "Many foods in rabbit diet are abrasive.", "Abrasive foods in rabbit diet cause attrition."], "filtered_facts_t": ["Rabbit teeth grow continuously throughout life.", "Many foods in rabbit diet are abrasive.", "Abrasive foods in rabbit diet cause attrition."], "accepted_facts_t": ["Rabbit teeth grow continuously throughout life.", "Many foods in rabbit diet are abrasive.", "Abrasive foods in rabbit diet cause attrition."], "delta_f": 0.9999999966666667, "novel_facts": ["Rabbit teeth grow continuously throughout life.", "Many foods in rabbit diet are abrasive.", "Abrasive foods in rabbit diet cause attrition."], "fact_novelty_matches": [{"fact": "Rabbit teeth grow continuously throughout life.", "is_novel": true, "duplicate_scope": null, "matched_fact": null, "matched_similarity": null}, {"fact": "Many foods in rabbit diet are abrasive.", "is_novel": true, "duplicate_scope": null, "matched_fact": null, "matched_similarity": null}, {"fact": "Abrasive foods in rabbit diet cause attrition.", "is_novel": true, "duplicate_scope": null, "matched_fact": null, "matched_similarity": null}], "cumulative_fact_count_after_dedup": 3, "delta_reason": "set_difference", "utility_label": "full_contribution", "utility": 1.0, "utility_reason": "The reasoning states that the evidence is sufficient to answer the needed subproblem directly, as it outlines the benefits of Western Timothy Hay for rabbit teeth including its high fiber and cellulose content and its role in preventing overgrowth through natural abrasion.", "step_score": 0.9999999966666667}]}
