{"id": "7f9bd8cc-ac5e-478b-84c0-48bbeacc3be8", "question": "solve this equation", "status": "ok", "num_iterations": 2, "total_delta_f": 0.0, "total_step_score": 0.0, "trajectory_quality_score": 0.0, "steps": [{"iteration_index": 1, "retrieval_action": "no_retrieval_result", "retrieval_type": "Text Retrieval", "mode": "no_retrieval", "previous_query_for_similarity": null, "query": "No Retrieval.", "query_similarity_enabled": true, "query_similarity_with_previous": null, "similarity_threshold": 0.85, "fact_similarity_threshold": 0.9, "retrieval_index": 3, "reaction_index": 4, "reaction_action": "thought", "reaction_text": "To solve the equation -6j + 6 = j + 3, I need to isolate the variable j on one side of the equation. I will start by subtracting j from both sides and then subtracting 6 from both sides to get all terms with j on one side and constants on the other.\n</Thought>", "facts_t": [], "filtered_facts_t": [], "accepted_facts_t": [], "delta_f": 0.0, "novel_facts": [], "fact_novelty_matches": [], "cumulative_fact_count_after_dedup": 0, "delta_reason": "no_contribution", "utility_label": "no_contribution", "utility": 0.0, "utility_reason": "The Next Reasoning Text explicitly indicates that the retrieval (if any) was skipped, and the model is proceeding with pure algebraic manipulation without using any retrieved facts. Since the facts list is empty and the reasoning makes no reference to external evidence, it aligns with cases where evidence is not used or irrelevant.", "step_score": 0.0}, {"iteration_index": 2, "retrieval_action": "no_retrieval_result", "retrieval_type": "Text Retrieval", "mode": "no_retrieval", "previous_query_for_similarity": "No Retrieval.", "query": "No Retrieval.", "query_similarity_enabled": true, "query_similarity_with_previous": 1.0, "similarity_threshold": 0.85, "fact_similarity_threshold": 0.9, "retrieval_index": 7, "reaction_index": 8, "reaction_action": "thought", "reaction_text": "To solve the equation -6j + 6 = j + 3, I will first subtract j from both sides to get all terms with j on one side:\n-6j - j + 6 = 3\nThis simplifies to:\n-7j + 6 = 3\nNext, I will subtract 6 from both sides to isolate the term with j:\n-7j = 3 - 6\nThis simplifies to:\n-7j = -3\nFinally, I will divide both sides by -7 to solve for j:\nj = -3 / -7\nThis simplifies to:\nj = 3 / 7\n</Thought>\n<Final Answer>\nThe solution to the equation -6j + 6 = j + 3 is j = 3/7.\n</Final Answer>", "facts_t": [], "filtered_facts_t": [], "accepted_facts_t": [], "delta_f": 0.0, "novel_facts": [], "fact_novelty_matches": [], "cumulative_fact_count_after_dedup": 0, "delta_reason": "similarity_gate", "utility_label": "no_contribution", "utility": 0.0, "utility_reason": "Similarity gate triggered because query similarity exceeded the threshold.", "step_score": 0.0}]}
